<%- include('partials/header', { title: title }) %>

<h1 tabindex="-1" data-autofocus><%= title %></h1>

<%- include('partials/status') %>

<% if (!request) { %>

  <p>
    There is no passkey replacement running on your account.
    <% if (sessionLevel === 'full') { %>
      Your passkeys are unchanged.
    <% } %>
  </p>
  <p><a href="/account">Go to your account</a></p>

<% } else if (!matured) { %>

  <h2>Waiting</h2>
  <%#
    The remaining time is written out in words and the exact moment is given
    in full. A ticking visual countdown would be unreadable to a screen reader
    and would keep interrupting it; WCAG 2.2 also asks that a time limit be
    something the user can actually understand and plan around.
  %>
  <p>
    You can register a new passkey after
    <strong><%= readyAt %></strong>. That is about
    <strong><%= remaining %></strong> from now.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing on your account has changed yet. Your existing passkeys still
    work, and we have told you about this request on your other contact
    channels.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/recover/status">Check the remaining time again</a> — the page
    does not refresh by itself.
  </p>

<% } else { %>

  <h2>Ready</h2>
  <p>
    The waiting period has finished. Register a new passkey below. When you
    do, <strong>every passkey currently on this account will be turned off</strong>
    and anything still signed in with one will be signed out.
  </p>

  <div class="prompt-notice">
    <h3>What happens when you select Register a new passkey</h3>
    <p>
      <strong><%= origin %></strong> will ask <strong>this device</strong>, or
      a security key you plug in, to create a passkey, then check it is you
      using your fingerprint, your face or your device PIN.
    </p>
  </div>

  <form id="replace-form" novalidate>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="device-name">A name for this passkey</label>
      <p class="hint" id="device-name-hint">
        Optional, for example “New phone”.
      </p>
      <input
        type="text"
        id="device-name"
        name="deviceName"
        aria-describedby="device-name-hint"
      />
    </div>
    <p><button type="submit" id="submit">Register a new passkey</button></p>
  </form>

<% } %>

<% if (request) { %>
  <h2>If this was not you</h2>
  <p>
    Cancelling stops the replacement. Your existing passkeys keep working and
    nothing is turned off.
  </p>
  <form method="post" action="/recover/cancel">
    <p><button class="danger" type="submit">Cancel this replacement</button></p>
  </form>
<% } %>

<%- include('partials/footer', { script: '/js/recover.js' }) %>
